A||||7||G-Nasty||Moan when low on gas?||||1||
Z||000000||G-Nasty||01-29-2001||12:00 AM||||Whats up the all the frik'n moaning? Why do these cars moan when they get low on gas...I know all mine do this-<BR>Make It Stop.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierosound||01-29-2001||01:27 AM||||It's the fuel pump sucking air.  It happens on other cars with in-tank electric pumps too, but you can't hear it when the tank is at the back of the car.  The Fiero's tank is in the center tunnel.  Mine also groans once I'm below 1/4 tank.  Time to fill-er-up... ||||reg||10
Z||000002||rogergarrison||01-29-2001||10:32 AM||||yep mine groans too when it gets between 1/8 and 1/4 tank. A lot of times im having so much fun i dont pay attention to gas gage, so i like it. I wouldnt even mind if it dinged for me.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TheFiero64||01-29-2001||11:14 AM||||Watch out! Its not good for the pump if you run it dry. It is lubricated by the fuel running through it.||||reg||4
Z||000004||2xsess||01-29-2001||12:06 PM||||I moan when I'm low on gas too.hehe<P>Mine is more of a whine from the pump though. I ignored it the first time and that was when I found out my gas gauge was a bit off.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">    <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||01-29-2001||06:52 PM||||Never noticed that on mine. I guess I was having too much fun driving this thing to notice.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||01-29-2001||07:47 PM||||The fuel pump vibrates as it runs. Fuel dampens the vibration. Once the fuel gets below a certain point there is not enough to dampen the vibration anymore and you hear it. Just if and when this happens depends on the specific pump. not all of them do it. The high pressure jobs like the V6 uses tend to do it more than the low pressure ones.<P>If the fuel pump was actually sucking air all that much the car would not run and you'd likely fry the pump.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Standard||01-30-2001||01:53 AM||||I usually moan when I'm full of gas...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I don't think I've ever heard either of my pumps moan, even right before I ran out of gas... my GT is still doing good, almost been a year since I ran it dry.  My 84 was doing fine when it got parked.||||reg||
